{% assign sj_key = key | plus: 0 %}{% case sj_key %}
{% when 1 %}{% case field %}
{% when 'title' %}Earrings and headphones: plan a workday that feels comfortable
{% when 'description' %}Choose earrings around the space your headphones leave, rather than a promise that one style suits every workday.
{% when 'direction' %}Presence &amp; comfort
{% when 'summary' %}Choose earrings around the space your headphones leave, rather than a promise that one style suits every workday. Check the ear cup, the post behind your ear, any hanging element and how often you take the headset on and off. A comfortable combination in a mirror can behave differently during a long call. The useful question is whether the two objects can move independently without pressing, catching or needing constant adjustment.
{% endcase %}
{% when 2 %}{% case field %}
{% when 'title' %}Why do earrings tilt forward? What to check before buying
{% when 'description' %}An earring that tilts forward needs a closer look at its whole arrangement: the front, post, back, position on the ear and any added ornament.
{% when 'direction' %}Presence &amp; comfort
{% when 'summary' %}An earring that tilts forward needs a closer look at its whole arrangement: the front, post, back, position on the ear and any added ornament. The number of grams alone does not explain the result. Before replacing a back or buying a larger one, identify what is moving and ask whether the parts are intended to work together. A photograph can help describe the tilt, but it cannot diagnose an ear or prove the cause.
{% endcase %}
{% when 3 %}{% case field %}
{% when 'title' %}Statement earrings on ordinary days: choosing your level of impact
{% when 'description' %}Statement earrings can belong to ordinary days when you choose the kind of presence you enjoy and the activities the pair must accommodate.
{% when 'direction' %}Presence &amp; comfort
{% when 'summary' %}Statement earrings can belong to ordinary days when you choose the kind of presence you enjoy and the activities the pair must accommodate. Begin with one familiar outfit, decide what you want the earrings to contribute, and check the complete arrangement in motion. There is no requirement to “dress up enough” for jewelry you like. There is also no obligation to wear a visually striking pair every day simply because you own it.
{% endcase %}
{% when 4 %}{% case field %}
{% when 'title' %}Will this ornament fit my SUIJI base?
{% when 'description' %}SUIJI ornaments fit bases equipped with the SUIJI multi-use clasp. Check the exact base, included pieces and any additional attachment.
{% when 'direction' %}Changing the details
{% when 'summary' %}Every SUIJI ornament fits every base equipped with the SUIJI multi-use clasp. Identify your base, count the included ornaments and check whether your chosen arrangement needs an additional attachment. A bare hoop and a completed clasp-equipped base are different products.
{% endcase %}
{% when 5 %}{% case field %}
{% when 'title' %}One base, two motifs: plan combinations you will actually wear
{% when 'description' %}Start a small interchangeable collection by planning two specific compositions, not by counting all the combinations theoretically possible.
{% when 'direction' %}Changing the details
{% when 'summary' %}Start a small interchangeable collection by planning two specific compositions, not by counting all the combinations theoretically possible. Choose a base for a real wearing position, name the job of each motif, and confirm the complete contents and compatibility. One base with two well-chosen ornaments can be useful; it can also be an unnecessary complication if you prefer one fixed piece. Your habits decide the value of the arrangement.
{% endcase %}
{% when 6 %}{% case field %}
{% when 'title' %}Interchangeable jewelry you never change: simplify the routine
{% when 'description' %}If you own interchangeable jewelry but rarely change it, start by finding the friction rather than buying another ornament.
{% when 'direction' %}Changing the details
{% when 'summary' %}If you own interchangeable jewelry but rarely change it, start by finding the friction rather than buying another ornament. You may prefer one settled composition, forget the alternatives, or find the handling awkward. Each situation suggests a different response. A fixed favorite is a valid outcome; the aim is to make the collection usable on your terms, not to reach a target number of changes.
{% endcase %}
{% when 7 %}{% case field %}
{% when 'title' %}From earring motif to pendant: what has to change?
{% when 'description' %}Moving an ornament from an earring to a necklace is a new configuration, not simply the same piece in a new photograph.
{% when 'direction' %}Ways to wear
{% when 'summary' %}Moving an ornament from an earring to a necklace is a new configuration, not simply the same piece in a new photograph. Confirm that the particular decorative element is intended for both positions, identify the required base or connector, and check how it hangs. Do not improvise a conversion from an earring post or assume an opening that accepts a chain makes the complete arrangement suitable.
{% endcase %}
{% when 8 %}{% case field %}
{% when 'title' %}Can a necklace become a bracelet? Fit, fastening and movement
{% when 'description' %}A necklace can serve as a bracelet only when its construction, fastening and fit support that use.
{% when 'direction' %}Ways to wear
{% when 'summary' %}A necklace can serve as a bracelet only when its construction, fastening and fit support that use. Length divided by wrist size is not enough to decide. The clasp needs to remain accessible, any ornament must sit as intended, and the arrangement must allow ordinary movement without becoming tight or liable to slip away. Do not turn a story about someone else’s successful wrap into a universal tutorial.
{% endcase %}
{% when 9 %}{% case field %}
{% when 'title' %}Convertible jewelry or separate pieces: which suits your habits?
{% when 'description' %}Choose convertible jewelry when its supported arrangements match situations you actually want and the change is easy enough for your routine.
{% when 'direction' %}Ways to wear
{% when 'summary' %}Choose convertible jewelry when its supported arrangements match situations you actually want and the change is easy enough for your routine. Choose separate pieces when you need simultaneous wear, distinct fits or fewer handling steps. Compare the complete objects, components and cost. The advertised number of “ways to wear” cannot tell you which option offers more value in your own life.
{% endcase %}
{% when 10 %}{% case field %}
{% when 'title' %}Small earring backs are hard to handle: questions for your next pair
{% when 'description' %}If small earring backs are difficult to handle, choose around the operation you need to perform: finding the part, holding it, aligning it and knowing it is engaged.
{% when 'direction' %}Fit &amp; handling
{% when 'summary' %}If small earring backs are difficult to handle, choose around the operation you need to perform: finding the part, holding it, aligning it and knowing it is engaged. A closure’s name alone does not tell you whether those steps will suit you. Ask to see the actual sequence and compare it with a piece you already use comfortably. More secure-sounding language is not a substitute for a mechanism you can operate as intended.
{% endcase %}
{% when 11 %}{% case field %}
{% when 'title' %}Buying hoops online: check the opening, post and closure
{% when 'description' %}Before buying hoops online, check the space inside the hoop, the post that enters the piercing and the way the closure opens and engages.
{% when 'direction' %}Fit &amp; handling
{% when 'summary' %}Before buying hoops online, check the space inside the hoop, the post that enters the piercing and the way the closure opens and engages. The outer diameter and a front photograph cannot answer all three questions. Compare the complete profile with a comfortable pair you already own, establish whether the listing sells one hoop or a pair, and ask about missing measurements before treating a size label as a fit recommendation.
{% endcase %}
{% when 12 %}{% case field %}
{% when 'title' %}Keep useful notes about jewelry comfort without guessing the cause
{% when 'description' %}Useful comfort notes record what you wore, how it was assembled, what you were doing and what you noticed.
{% when 'direction' %}Fit &amp; handling
{% when 'summary' %}Useful comfort notes record what you wore, how it was assembled, what you were doing and what you noticed. They do not assign a cause. Keep the record brief and factual, and do not keep wearing uncomfortable jewelry to complete it. For a concerning or new symptom, seek appropriate professional advice promptly; a diary is a communication aid, not a substitute for assessment or a reason to delay help.
{% endcase %}
{% when 13 %}{% case field %}
{% when 'title' %}Buying yourself jewelry: choose a piece for the life you have
{% when 'description' %}Buy yourself jewelry by choosing the role you want it to have, then a budget and a piece that suits that role.
{% when 'direction' %}Gifts &amp; memories
{% when 'summary' %}Buy yourself jewelry by choosing the role you want it to have, then a budget and a piece that suits that role. A milestone can be a reason, but it is not a requirement. You do not need another person to authorize the meaning, or a luxury category to make the purchase legitimate. The practical question is whether the piece fits your life and a cost you are comfortable accepting.
{% endcase %}
{% when 14 %}{% case field %}
{% when 'title' %}Sentimental jewelry you do not wear: keep the meaning, choose the role
{% when 'description' %}Sentimental jewelry does not have to earn its place through frequent wear.
{% when 'direction' %}Gifts &amp; memories
{% when 'summary' %}Sentimental jewelry does not have to earn its place through frequent wear. First decide whether you want to preserve the object, the memory, a recognizable feature or the possibility of wearing it differently. Then choose a reversible next step where possible. Keeping a piece safely stored, asking about repair, adapting a supported component or considering a professional redesign are different decisions; none needs to be made because a wardrobe rule says unused jewelry must go.
{% endcase %}
{% when 15 %}{% case field %}
{% when 'title' %}Choose a jewelry gift without guessing someone’s style
{% when 'description' %}A useful jewelry gift begins with the recipient’s actual habits, not a universal “safe” style.
{% when 'direction' %}Gifts &amp; memories
{% when 'summary' %}A useful jewelry gift begins with the recipient’s actual habits, not a universal “safe” style. Notice what they wear, ask about important unknowns and choose how much surprise to preserve. Confirm quantity, complete contents, fit information and the seller’s actual gift or return conditions. A thoughtful choice can be a piece selected together; guessing is not a requirement for generosity.
{% endcase %}
{% when 16 %}{% case field %}
{% when 'title' %}A charm collection with memories and room to breathe
{% when 'description' %}Build a memory-charm collection by separating the stories you want to keep from the ornaments you want to wear together.
{% when 'direction' %}Gifts &amp; memories
{% when 'summary' %}Build a memory-charm collection by separating the stories you want to keep from the ornaments you want to wear together. Every meaningful element does not need to be on one base at once. Choose a small current composition, retain the other pieces with their references and stories, and confirm compatibility whenever you change the arrangement. A collection can remain emotionally complete while its worn version stays simple.
{% endcase %}
{% when 17 %}{% case field %}
{% when 'title' %}How to write a custom jewelry brief a maker can use
{% when 'description' %}A useful custom-jewelry brief tells a maker what you want to wear, what matters visually, what must fit and what you are prepared to spend.
{% when 'direction' %}Your own design
{% when 'summary' %}A useful custom-jewelry brief tells a maker what you want to wear, what matters visually, what must fit and what you are prepared to spend. It leaves technical solutions open for discussion. Start with ordinary use and a few priorities, not a request to copy another designer’s exact piece. The aim is a shared decision document that makes questions and trade-offs visible before production begins.
{% endcase %}
{% when 18 %}{% case field %}
{% when 'title' %}How to review a jewelry CAD rendering before approval
{% when 'description' %}Review a jewelry rendering as one version of a proposed design, alongside dimensions, component information and an agreed production process.
{% when 'direction' %}Your own design
{% when 'summary' %}Review a jewelry rendering as one version of a proposed design, alongside dimensions, component information and an agreed production process. Begin with scale and structure, then orientation and surface details, and finally the questions the image cannot answer. Do not approve a commission simply because the lighting looks convincing. A photorealistic image is not a physical fitting, material certificate or guarantee that an object can be made exactly as shown.
{% endcase %}
{% when 19 %}{% case field %}
{% when 'title' %}Custom jewelry revisions: agree scope, cost and approval stages
{% when 'description' %}Agree a custom-jewelry revision by identifying the current version, the exact change, its effect on price and timing, and what your approval authorizes next.
{% when 'direction' %}Your own design
{% when 'summary' %}Agree a custom-jewelry revision by identifying the current version, the exact change, its effect on price and timing, and what your approval authorizes next. Keep design discussion separate from permission to start an irreversible production step. A clear process cannot guarantee the result, but it can prevent both parties from working from different assumptions about what is included or already approved.
{% endcase %}
{% when 20 %}{% case field %}
{% when 'title' %}Before redesigning heirloom jewelry: decide what must survive
{% when 'description' %}Before redesigning heirloom jewelry, decide what must survive, have the actual object assessed, and agree which steps are reversible.
{% when 'direction' %}Your own design
{% when 'summary' %}Before redesigning heirloom jewelry, decide what must survive, have the actual object assessed, and agree which steps are reversible. Preserve a record before any component is removed or altered. A new wearable piece can retain part of a story, but it may not retain the original object, workmanship or all its value. The useful first decision is what you are willing to change, not which attractive new setting to copy.
{% endcase %}
{% endcase %}